---
import DrawbridgeLayout from "@/layouts/DrawbridgeLayout.astro";
---

<DrawbridgeLayout
  title="Outcome Mapper quick-start"
  description="Get started with the Outcome Mapper tool."
>
  <article class="grid gap-8">
    <div class="grid gap-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Outcome Mapper: Quick-start</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground">Load outcomes, create mappings, and export an alignment table.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="grid gap-6 list-decimal pl-5">
      <li class="pl-2">
        <strong>Open the tool.</strong> Go to
        <a href="/tools/outcome-mapper" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary-accent">Outcome Mapper</a>.
      </li>
      <li class="pl-2">
        <strong>Prepare your data.</strong> Create a table with columns <code>level</code>, <code>id</code>, and
        <code>text</code>. Optionally add a <code>mapsTo</code> column with comma-separated parent ids.
        <pre class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border bg-muted/50 p-3 text-xs">level,id,text,mapsTo
program,po1,Communicate effectively,
course,co1,Write clear arguments,po1
assessment,ao1,Thesis is clear,co1</pre>
      </li>
      <li class="pl-2">
        <strong>Load the outcomes.</strong> Paste the table into the input area and click <strong>Load outcomes</strong>.
        Notes about any formatting issues appear below the input.
      </li>
      <li class="pl-2">
        <strong>Create mappings.</strong> For each lower-level outcome, check the box next to the higher-level outcomes
        it supports. Program-level outcomes have no higher level to map to.
      </li>
      <li class="pl-2">
        <strong>Export.</strong> Click <strong>Continue to export</strong>, then download the alignment table or the
        updated outcome list.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </article>
</DrawbridgeLayout>
